DESCRIPTION:<b>For employees of Duke University and DUHS.</b>\n<b>Continui
 ng Education Credits (CEUs)</b>: 0.3\n\nUsing social capital as a focusin
 g concept\, the class highlights the importance of communication for buil
 ding positive and productive working relationships. At the end of the cou
 rse participants will be able to recognize patterns of communication\, id
 entify strengths and weaknesses of current communication practices\, and 
 develop new or improved communication strategies with coworkers and those
  in other departments.\n \n<b>Assessment</b>: The Myer's-Briggs Type Indi
 cator® (MBTI®) assessment will be debriefed during this session\; all par
 ticipants must complete the assessment at least two weeks prior to the st
 art of the course.
